From 336a93b8642d19852d9b64f9de32b04f4622d0c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zak Wilson <zak.wilson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:10:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Add variadic functions: :varargs, VaList, unsafe/va-arg,
 va-copy (VA-1..VA-6)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`defn`, `declare` and function-pointer types take `:varargs`, and a plain
`declare` is exact (Q2): a tail on one is an error naming `:varargs`.
`VaList` is a `ptr` in IR set apart by its own pointee; on a cursor target the
call path loads it and the prologue spills it. `va_list` in a C header imports
as one. Every refusal of §4.1 is a diagnostic.

LLVM's `va_arg` turned out wrong on AAPCS and, at -O0, broken on x86-64 too (the
fast allocator reloads a spill it never wrote), so both aggregate classes are
open-coded in `select`s. A redefinable variadic works at the REPL via musttail.

design/lua-bugfixes/variadic-functions.md, Status, has the as-built differences.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
